[stderr] +Allocate only newly ready, unassigned catalogue contracts. Create at most ten
[stderr] +B tasks and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit B task.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Validation procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Validate JSON, the selected chapter limit, monotonic unique IMP/B/R IDs,
[stderr] +dependency closure/acyclicity, output ownership, provenance, allocation
[stderr] +uniqueness, asset metadata, and B limits. Verify the successor/final choice
[stderr] +against remaining queue and ready contracts.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Checkpoint and update procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Update JSON and Markdown ledgers only after validation. Retain IDs on repair;
[stderr] +never overwrite, renumber, or regenerate accepted B/R work.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Collision protection
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Before creating an ID or path, verify it is absent from the manifest and
[stderr] +filesystem. Stop on a collision or unresolved authority.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Stop condition
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Stop after one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and exactly one
[stderr] +successor or audit task; do not recursively materialise later work.
