+through `#5-inventory-party-progression-and-economy`, and
+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract` plus
+`#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`
+and F014 provenance/asset rules.
+
+## Output list
+
+- `../runbooks/R0013.md` — IMP-0013.
+- `../runbooks/R0014.md` — IMP-0014.
+- `../runbooks/R0015.md` — IMP-0015.
+- `../runbooks/R0016.md` — IMP-0016.
+
+## Validation procedure
+
+Before writing, confirm each path is absent or is this batch's repair target;
+never overwrite accepted work. Compare front matter, requirement IDs,
+dependencies, ownership, provenance, factory stages, and asset assessment to
+the manifest. Include all standard contract sections, `## Verification`, and
+`## Asset assessment`; retain GATE-0004 rather than resolving it.
+
+## Checkpoint and update procedure
+
+After each valid R file, record the result in the B0007 checkpoint/state only.
+On failure retain R0013–R0016 and repair only the failed assigned path, then
+rerun the structural validator through B0007.
+
+## Collision protection
+
+Check manifest ID/path ownership and the filesystem before every output. Stop
+on a duplicate ID, output path, provenance mismatch, or conflicting accepted
+contract; do not renumber or reallocate.
+
+## Stop condition
+
+Stop after these four R outputs. Do not author B0008 outputs, allocate IDs, or
+create product assets.
