`../runbooks/R0018.md` \u2014 IMP-0018.\n+- `../runbooks/R0019.md` \u2014 IMP-0019.\n+- `../runbooks/R0020.md` \u2014 IMP-0020.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, confirm no accepted path will be overwritten. Match each R\n+front matter, requirement IDs, dependencies, ownership, canonical provenance,\n+factory stages, and asset metadata to the manifest. Every R includes standard\n+sections, `## Verification`, and `## Asset assessment`; asset-required R0018\n+must name only its reserved stable asset IDs and prohibit creation in authoring.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint only validated assigned files. Retain R0017\u2013R0020 on failure and\n+repair only the failing output before rerunning the structural validator through\n+B0008; never treat implementation gates as authoring approval.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Check manifest and filesystem ownership before each write. Stop for duplicate\n+IDs/paths, dependency/provenance mismatch, missing asset assessment, or a\n+conflict with accepted work; do not renumber or reallocate.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these four outputs. Do not author a UI/PWA contract, allocate more\n+work, or create the reserved product assets.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2ec7da8cb5892e7ee37dc61faaa21641a5f4fc83\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0003\n+sequence: 12\n+title: Continue bounded implementation-runbook authoring dispatch after SHARD-02\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable dispatch iteration after D0002: expand at most one eligible\n+queued chapter into no more than 250 IMP records, allocate ready unassigned\n+contracts to at most ten B batches of at most seven R outputs, then create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher while queue/ready work remains, otherwise one\n+final audit B task.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the canonical specification, catalogue,\n+authoritative JSON/Markdown manifest, D0002 checkpoint, and F014. Gates remain\n+explicit implementation constraints; SHARD-05 remains held without recorded\n+authorisation.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+Allocate only newly ready, unassigned catalogue contracts. Create at most ten\n+B tasks and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit B task.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the selected chapter limit, monotonic unique IMP/B/R IDs,\n+dependency closure/acyclicity, output ownership, provenance, allocation\n+uniqueness, asset metadata, and B limits. Verify the successor/final choice\n+against remaining queue and ready contracts.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update JSON and Markdown ledgers only after validation. Retain IDs on repair;\n+never overwrite, renumber, or regenerate accepted B/R work.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Before creating an ID or path, verify it is absent from the manifest and\n+filesystem. Stop on a collision or unresolved authority.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and exactly one\n+successor or audit task; do not recursively materialise later work.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\nindex 8658e5ee05d7f524f0320681a1d98c40f8af61fb..ad08afa1de94c10a08199c09b206dec8b95d9615\n--- a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n@@ -4,1